# Module Catalog

Owns the shipped module identifiers, their minimum plan tier, and which permission
domains they gate. Seed only modules from this catalog.

Canonical source: `backend/src/lib/subscriptions/plan-module-matrix.js` — 29 commercial
entries grouped by `minimum_plan_tier_code`, plus 4 platform infrastructure entries.
Nothing here may be edited without changing that file; the tables below describe it, they
are not a second catalog.

## Two identifiers, one module

Every module carries both. Confusing them is the most common bug in this area.

- `code` — snake_case (`inpatient_bed_management`). Seed/backfill identity only.
- `slug` — kebab-case (`inpatient-bed-management`). **The runtime identifier.** Module
  entitlements, `activeModules` requirements in frontend access files, and the
  permission→module map all use the slug.

`normalizeModuleCode` lowercases and converts `_`/whitespace to `-`, so a code will
usually resolve, but always write the slug. One pair is deliberately mismatched:
code `mortuary_operations` has slug `mortuary`.

## Module keys are not permission domains

A module is not a screen and not a permission prefix. Several domains share one module,
and the names differ:

- `reception`, `opd` and `emergency` → `scheduling-queue`
- `ipd`, `nursing`, `discharge` and `rooms_beds` → `inpatient-bed-management`
- `hr`, `unit` and `roster` → `hr-rosters`
- `operations` and `housekeeping` → `facilities-maintenance`
- `billing` and `financial` → `billing-payments`
- `patient` and `patients` → `patient-registry`

Mapping lives in `DOMAIN_TO_MODULE` (`backend/src/lib/authorization/permission-module-map.js`,
31 domains), mirrored in `frontend/lib/core/permissions/permission_module_map.dart`. The
two must stay identical. The remaining 11 domains are core/platform — see
`permissions.mdc`.

`pricing:*` is deliberately **not** in the map. It is a rights-layer permission that
crosses modules: the Billing price book (gated by `billing-payments`) hosts both facility
tariff rows and pharmacy retail rows, so `pricing:pharmacy_write` must work there without
requiring `pharmacy-dispensing`. The screen is module-gated; the permission is not.

## Platform infrastructure modules

Always entitled, on every package. Not sellable, not removable. Each carries
`extension_json.is_platform_infrastructure = true` and an `api_path_segments` list that
`module-entitlement.middleware.js` reads to let those routes through.

| Slug | Code | Min tier | Permission domains |
| ---- | ---- | -------- | ------------------ |
| `platform-identity` | `platform_identity` | FREE | — (entitlement only) |
| `platform-facility-structure` | `platform_facility_structure` | FREE | — (entitlement only) |
| `platform-workspace-shell` | `platform_workspace_shell` | FREE | — (entitlement only) |
| `reporting-analytics` | `reporting_analytics` | FREE | `reports` |

`reporting-analytics` is special-cased in `isPermissionAllowedByPlan`: it passes the module
gate regardless of entitlement rows, so reporting is available on every package.

